// x17 "Seat Swap" (script v2, 2026-10-27, docs/x17-seat-swap.md). Ross 10-27: "now make the next cartoon ... just see it through to the end and send me the finished reel, from a viral script"; pitch 2 of docs/ideas-viral-2026-10.md (the plane seat swap, the biggest fight in our TikTok search).
// Ross paid for window seat 12A; a honeymoon couple asks him to swap, a support peacock takes his middle seat, the attendant sucks him out onto the wing and charges him for the legroom; he blows, the pilot takes the wing and hands him the plane, and the couple pops up again.
// Ross is jack-tyler (as in x08-x16), the bride Jessica, the groom Will, the flight attendant Bella, the pilot Brian. No swearing in this one.
// The couple's "Hiii!" is two lines said together (2 and 3, 13 and 14): a negative gap puts the groom's take on the bride's.
// Format: see scripts/voice-gen.mjs (lines, directions) and scripts/voice-build.py (cast, plan, gaps, lead, tableSfx). Take k of a line uses direction k.
{
 "title": "Seat Swap",
 "cast": {"ross": 1, "bride": 1, "groom": 1, "fa": 1, "pilot": 1},
 "runnerUp": {},
 "lines": [
// cheek on the window, blissful, the boarding pass on his tray
